findings.verifierNote:
Confirmed major. Reproduced on HEAD with an independent decomposition: the same 18 slots fail, plus a hidden false pass (Kemdo a3).

I tried to refute it on metric grounds:
- the luma threshold disfavours dark blue/violet signatures;
- the max-n frame favours big rings;
- warm light on brown stone measures as HARM hue.

The team/signature blackout settles it. Team-keyed light really is 36-95 % on 9 slots, and on the neutral-carried slots signature layers add about 0 % of the light. Frame-integrated and chroma-weighted shares fail the same slots.

Two descriptive slips do not change the verdict:
- Tunlan's 'orange rims' is the legitimate cone telegraph;
- Ilsheta is mostly warm white, not orange.

Major is right: this is r12 M12 (a major) on half of every kit, including the ultimate.

